    <statement><p>Let <m>p</m> be the joint density function such
that <m>p(x,y) = \frac{1}{9} xy</m> in <m>R</m>, the rectangle
<m>0 \le x \le 6, 0\le y \le 1</m>, and <m>p(x,y)=0</m>
outside <m>R</m>.  Find the fraction of the population
satisfying the constraint
<m>x+y \le 7</m></p>
<p>fraction = <fillin characters="35" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>1</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>x+y \le 7</m> for all points <m>(x,y)</m>  in the region
<m>R</m>, the fraction of the population satisfying <m>x+y \le 7</m>
is 1.




</solution>
